# Internet reading for 07/2026

A shortlist of things on the internet I enjoyed reading in June.


- [A Voice From Nowhere](https://zanlib.dev/blog/a-voice-from-nowhere/)

- [The Night Feeling](https://cleberg.net/blog/the-night-feeling.html)

- [Protect Your Friends and Loved Ones](https://ephemeral.cx/2026/07/protect-your-friends-and-loved-ones/) --- A good read about [OPSEC](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operational_security), and being prepared. (Mostly US-centric).

- [Simple rules for a happier life](https://jagasantagostino.com/blog/simple-rules-for-a-happier-life) --- Two very simple rules.

- [How to read more books](https://scotto.me/blog/2026-07-12-how-to-read-more-books/) --- Ironically I don't think I read this one in its entirety.

- [A Scent of Twilight](https://rootmap.bearblog.dev/a-scent-of-twilight/) -- Enjoyable prose.

- [Journalist Richard Medhurst had his mobile phone seized. Did using a secure phone protect his data?](https://www.computerweekly.com/feature/Journalist-Richard-Medhurst-had-his-mobile-phone-seized-Did-using-a-secure-phone-protect-his-data) --- Another one about OPSEC. To my knowledge, the first documented case of [GrapheneOS](https://grapheneos.org/) helping a journalist. 

- [US government targets Cop City protester over phone operating system](https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jul/23/cop-city-protester-phone) --- Another one about GrapheneOS in the wild.

- [Week 29, 2026: The slow build](https://zeina.bearblog.dev/week-29-2026/) --- Enjoyable prose.

- [Don't talk to me about AI: I will shit myself](https://halcyondays.bearblog.dev/dont-talk-to-me-about-ai-i-will-shit-myself/)
